WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.832
FedRAMP stands for the Federal Risk and Authorization Management Program.

00:00:03.832 --> 00:00:08.311
It is a United States government program that standardizes security assessment, authorization,

00:00:08.311 --> 00:00:12.043
and continuous monitoring for cloud services used by federal agencies.

00:00:12.043 --> 00:00:13.909
The basic purpose is consistency.

00:00:13.909 --> 00:00:17.642
Before FedRAMP, agencies could evaluate cloud services in different ways,

00:00:17.642 --> 00:00:20.254
which created duplicated work and uneven expectations.

00:00:20.254 --> 00:00:22.494
FedRAMP gives agencies, cloud providers, assessors,

00:00:22.494 --> 00:00:25.106
and stakeholders a shared process and vocabulary.

00:00:25.106 --> 00:00:30.705
FedRAMP matters because federal agencies rely on cloud services to support mission and business functions.

00:00:30.705 --> 00:00:34.064
Those services may process, store, or transmit government information,

00:00:34.064 --> 00:00:38.916
so agencies need a structured way to understand and manage cloud security risk.

00:00:38.916 --> 00:00:42.648
FedRAMP is not simply a form or a product label.

00:00:42.648 --> 00:00:46.007
It combines security controls, documentation, independent assessment, authorization decisions,

00:00:46.007 --> 00:00:50.486
and ongoing monitoring into a repeatable program for federal cloud risk management.

00:00:50.486 --> 00:00:54.964
A cloud service provider may use FedRAMP to demonstrate that its cloud

00:00:54.964 --> 00:00:58.323
offering has been assessed against common federal security expectations.

00:00:58.323 --> 00:01:03.175
Agencies can then use that information as part of their own risk decisions.

00:01:03.175 --> 00:01:08.027
The program is built on NIST guidance, especially NIST SP 800-53 security controls.

00:01:08.027 --> 00:01:13.253
That connection helps FedRAMP align with broader federal information security and risk management practices.

00:01:13.253 --> 00:01:16.612
This course provides an educational overview of FedRAMP concepts.

00:01:16.612 --> 00:01:20.717
It should not be used as professional legal, compliance, authorization, assessment,

00:01:20.717 --> 00:01:21.837
or regulatory direction.

00:01:21.837 --> 00:01:27.062
The most useful way to think about FedRAMP is as a shared trust mechanism.

00:01:27.062 --> 00:01:29.301
It gives cloud providers, federal agencies,

00:01:29.301 --> 00:01:33.780
and assessors a common way to organize evidence and discuss security posture.
